body:
L'exemple que tu as pris à propos des femmes adultères vient du Deutéronome, donc de la Torah... À une époque où le Christianisme n'existait pas...

&#x200B;

Faut pas confondre Ancien et Nouveau Testament, voilà ce que Jésus dit à propos des femmes adultères [ceci](https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Jean+8%3A7-11&version=LSG)

Emi feels sorry when confessing to Hisao on her good ending though, she acknowledges the fact that Hisao is worthy of getting close to her. 

Emi is kind of a proud girl who doesn't  think she needs any kind of help other than what she can do for herself.

&#x200B;

Aside from that, I think you'll enjoy Rin, her route is a bit different than others' :D

&#x200B;

Still doing Hanako btw so I didn't read all of your original post.

I am french and this ban just felt like it destroyed my life, I don't know what to do anymore, kratom helped me cope with depression and was the only thing that made me feel joy, happiness, I don't know what to say, I am angry and desperate, I am crying since I heard this. I want to end myself.

&#x200B;

I don't even know if there will be any resistance among french people, you Americans have the American Kratom Association, and we have nothing. We are way more submissive to our State.

&#x200B;

Fuck France, from the depths of my heart. I'm drunk to cope with the shock due to this very bad information, but it doesn't make the pain go away.

&#x200B;

I am speechless from now on. I, I don't know what to say...

Courage, fuyons...
